{
  "title": "26: Ash-Shu'ara الشعراء",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nطٰسٓمّٓ‏(1)\nTAA SIM MEEM.\nTa, Seen, Meem.\nتِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ الْكِتٰبِ الْمُبِيْنِ‏(2)\nTILKA AAYAATUL KETAABIL MOBEEN.\nThese are the signs of the Manifest Book.\nلَعَلَّكَ بَاخِعٌ نَّفْسَكَ اَلَّا يَكُوْنُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(3)\nLA-A’LLAKA BAAKHE-U’N NAFSAKA ALLAA YAKOONOO MOAMENEEN.\nYou are liable to imperil your life [out of distress] that they will not have faith.\nاِنْ نَّشَاْ نُنَزِّلْ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ اٰيَةً فَظَلَّتْ اَعْنَاقُهُمْ لَهَا خٰضِعِيْنَ‏(4)\nIN NASHAA NONAZZIL A’LAYHIM MENAS SAMAAA-E AAYATAN FA-ZALLAT A-A’NAAQOHUM LAHAA KHAAZE-E’EN.\nIf We wish We will send down to them a sign from the sky before which their heads will remain bowed in humility.\nوَمَا يَاْتِيْهِمْ مِّنْ ذِكْرٍ مِّنَ الرَّحْمٰنِ مُحْدَثٍ اِلَّا كَانُوْا عَنْهُ مُعْرِضِيْنَ‏(5)\nWA MAA YAATEEHIM MIN ZIKRIM MENAR RAHMAANE MOHDASIN ILLAA KAANOO A’NHO MO’REZEEN.\nThere does not come to them any new reminder from the All-beneficent but that they disregard it.\nفَقَدْ كَذَّبُوْا فَسَيَاْتِيْهِمْ اَنْۢبٰٓؤُا مَا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(6)\nFAQAD KAZZABOO FASAYAATEEHIM AMBAAA-O MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZE-OON.\nThey have already denied [the truth], but soon there will come to them the news of what they have been deriding.\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اِلَى الْاَرْضِ كَمْ اَنْۢبَتْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ زَوْجٍ كَرِيْمٍ‏(7)\nAWA LAM YARAW ELAL ARZE KAM AMBATNAA FEEHAA MIN KULLE ZAWJIN KAREEM.\nHave they not regarded the earth, how many of every splendid kind [of vegetation] We have caused to grow in it?\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً‌  ؕ وَّمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(8)\nINNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAH, WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nThere is indeed a sign in that; but most of them do not have faith.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(9)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUR RAHEEM.\nIndeed your Lord is the All-mighty, the All-merciful.\nوَاِذْ نَادٰى رَبُّكَ مُوْسٰۤى اَنِ ائْتِ الْقَوْمَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(10)\nWA IZ NAADAA RABBOKA MOOSAA ANEATIL QAWMAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nWhen your Lord called out to Moses: [saying,] ‘Go to those wrongdoing people,\nقَوْمَ فِرْعَوْنَ‌ؕ اَلَا يَتَّقُوْنَ‌‏(11)\nQAWMA FIR-A’WN, ALAA YATTAQOON.\nthe people of Pharaoh. Will they not be wary [of Allah]?’\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اَنْ يُّكَذِّبُوْنِؕ‏(12)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE AKHAAFO AN-Y YOKAZZEBOON.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! I fear they will impugn me,\nوَيَضِيْقُ صَدْرِىْ وَلَا يَنْطَلِقُ لِسَانِىْ فَاَرْسِلْ اِلٰى هٰرُوْنَ‏(13)\nWA YAZEEQO SADREE WA LAA YANTALEQO LESAANEE FA-ARSIL ELAA HAAROON.\nand I will become upset and my tongue will fail me. So send for Aaron [to join me].\nوَلَهُمْ عَلَىَّ ذَنْۢبٌ فَاَخَافُ اَنْ يَّقْتُلُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(14)\nWA LAHUM A’LAYYA ZAMBUN FA-AKHAAFO AN-Y YAQTOLOON.\nBesides, they have a charge against me, and I fear they will kill me.’\nقَالَ كَلَّا‌ ۚ فَاذْهَبَا بِاٰيٰتِنَآ‌ اِنَّا مَعَكُمْ مُّسْتَمِعُوْنَ‏(15)\nQAALA KALLAA, FAZHABAA BE-AAYAATENAA INNAA MA-A’KUM MUSTAME-O’ON.\nHe said, ‘Certainly not! Let both of you go with Our signs: We will indeed be with you, hearing [everything].\nفَاْتِيَا فِرْعَوْنَ فَقُوْلَاۤ اِنَّا رَسُوْلُ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(16)\nFAATEYAA FIR-A’WNA FA-QOOLAA INNAA RASOOLO RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nSo approach Pharaoh and say, ‘‘We are indeed envoys of the Lord of the worlds\nاَنْ اَرْسِلْ مَعَنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ ؕ‏(17)\nAN ARSIL MA-A’NAA BANEE ISRAAA-EEL.\nthat you let the Children of Israel leave with us.’’ ’\nقَالَ اَلَمْ نُرَبِّكَ فِيْنَا وَلِيْدًا وَّلَبِثْتَ فِيْنَا مِنْ عُمُرِكَ سِنِيْنَۙ‏(18)\nQAALA ALAM NORABBEKA FEENAA WALEEDANW WA LABISTA FEENAA MIN O’MOREKA SENEEN.\nHe [i.e. Pharaoh] said, ‘Did we not rear you as a child among us, and did you not stay with us for years of your life?\nوَفَعَلْتَ فَعْلَتَكَ الَّتِىْ فَعَلْتَ وَاَنْتَ مِنَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(19)\nWA FA-A’LTA FA’LATAKAL LATEE FA-A’LTA WA ANTA MENAL KAAFEREEN.\nThen you committed that deed of yours, and you are an ingrate.’\nقَالَ فَعَلْتُهَاۤ اِذًا وَّاَنَا مِنَ الضَّآلِّيْنَؕ‏(20)\nQAALA FA-A’LTOHAA EZANW WA ANAA MENAZ ZAALLEEN.\nHe said, ‘I did that when I was astray.\nفَفَرَرْتُ مِنْكُمْ لَمَّا خِفْتُكُمْ فَوَهَبَ لِىْ رَبِّىْ حُكْمًا وَّجَعَلَنِىْ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(21)\nFA-FARARTO MINKUM LAMMAA KHIFTOKUM FA-WAHABA LEE RABBEE HUKMANW WA JA-A’LANEE MENAL MURSALEEN.\nSo I fled from you, as I was afraid of you. Then my Lord gave me sound judgement and made me one of the apostles.\nوَتِلْكَ نِعْمَةٌ تَمُنُّهَا عَلَىَّ اَنْ عَبَّدْتَّ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ ؕ‏(22)\nWA TILKA NE’MATUN TAMUNNOHAA A’LAYYA AN A’BBATTA BANEE ISRAAA-EEL.\nThat you have enslaved the Children of Israel—is that the favour with which you reproach me?’\nقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ وَمَا رَبُّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(23)\nQAALA FIR-A’WNO WA MAA RABBUL A’ALAMEEN.\nHe said, ‘And what is ‘‘the Lord of all the worlds?’’ ’\nقَالَ رَبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَاؕ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّوْقِنِيْنَ‏(24)\nQAALA RABBUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA, IN KUNTUM MOOQENEEN.\nHe said, ‘The Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them,—should you have conviction.’\nقَالَ لِمَنْ حَوْلَهٗۤ اَلَا تَسْتَمِعُوْنَ‏(25)\nQAALA LEMAN HAWLAHU ALAA TASTAME-O’ON.\nHe said to those who were around him, ‘Don’t you hear?!’\nقَالَ رَبُّكُمْ وَرَبُّ اٰبَآئِكُمُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(26)\nQAALA RABBOKUM WA RABBO AABAAA-EKOMUL AWWALEEN.\nHe said, ‘Your Lord, and the Lord of your forefathers!’\nقَالَ اِنَّ رَسُوْلَكُمُ الَّذِىْۤ اُرْسِلَ اِلَيْكُمْ لَمَجْنُوْنٌ‏(27)\nQAALA INNA RASOOLAKOMUL LAZEE URSELA ELAYKUM LA-MAJNOON.\nHe said, ‘Indeed your messenger, who has been sent to you, is surely crazy!’\nقَالَ رَبُّ الْمَشْرِقِ وَالْمَغْرِبِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا ؕ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(28)\nQAALA RABBUL MASHREQE WAL MAGHREBE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA, IN KUNTUM TA’QELOON.\nHe said, ‘The Lord of the east and the west and whatever is between them—should you exercise your reason.’\nقَالَ لَئِنِ اتَّخَذْتَ اِلٰهًا غَيْرِىْ لَاَجْعَلَنَّكَ مِنَ الْمَسْجُوْنِيْنَ‏(29)\nQAALA LA-ENIT TAKHAZTA ELAAHAN GHAYREE LA-AJ-A’LANNAKA MENAL MASJOONEEN.\nHe said, ‘If you take up any god other than me, I will surely make you a prisoner!’\nقَالَ اَوَلَوْ جِئْتُكَ بِشَىْءٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‌ۚ‏(30)\nQAALA AWA LAW JEATOKA BE-SHAY-IM MOBEEN.\nHe said, ‘What if I bring you something [as an] unmistakable [proof]?’\nقَالَ فَاْتِ بِهٖۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(31)\nQAALA FAATE BEHI IN KUNTA MENAS SAADEQEEN.\nHe said, ‘Then bring it, should you be truthful.’\n‌فَاَ لْقٰى عَصَاهُ فَاِذَا هِىَ ثُعْبَانٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‌ ۖ ‌‌ۚ‏(32)\nFA-ALQAA A’SAAHO FA-EZAA HEYA SO’BAANUM MOBEEN.\nThereat he threw down his staff, and behold, it was a manifest python.\nوَّنَزَعَ يَدَهٗ فَاِذَا هِىَ بَيْضَآءُ لِلنّٰظِرِيْنَ‏(33)\nWA NAZA-A’ YADAHU FA-EZAA HEYA BAYZAAA-O LIN-NAAZEREEN.\nThen he drew out his hand, and behold, it was white and bright to the onlookers.\nقَالَ لِلْمَلَاِ حَوْلَهٗۤ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَسٰحِرٌ عَلِيْمٌۙ‏(34)\nQAALA LIL-MALA-E HAWLAHU INNA HAAZAA LA-SAAHERUN A’LEEM.\nHe said to the elite [who stood] around him, ‘This is indeed an expert magician\nيُّرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّخْرِجَكُمْ مِّنْ اَرْضِكُمْ بِسِحْرِهٖ ‌ۖ  فَمَاذَا تَاْمُرُوْنَ‌‏(35)\nYOREEDO AN-Y YUKHREJAKUM MIN ARZEKUM BE-SEHREH, FAMAAZAA TAAMOROON.\nwho seeks to expel you from your land with his magic. So what do you advise?’\nقَالُوْۤا اَرْجِهْ وَاَخَاهُ وَابْعَثْ فِى الْمَدَآئِنِ حٰشِرِيْنَۙ‏(36)\nQAALOO ARJEH WA AKHAAHO WAB A’S FIL MADAAA-ENE HAASHEREEN.\nThey said, ‘Put him and his brother off for a while, and send heralds to the cities\nيَاْتُوْكَ بِكُلِّ سَحَّارٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(37)\nYAATOOKA BE-KULLE SAHHAARIN A’LEEM.\nto bring you every expert magician.’\nفَجُمِعَ السَّحَرَةُ لِمِيْقَاتِ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُوْمٍۙ‏(38)\nFA-JOME-A’S SAHARATO LE-MEEQAATE YAWMIM MA’LOOM.\nSo the magicians were gathered for the tryst of a known day,\nوَّقِيْلَ لِلنَّاسِ هَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّجْتَمِعُوْنَۙ‏(39)\nWA QEELA LIN-NAASE HAL ANTUM MUJTAME-O’ON.\nand the people were told: ‘Will you all gather?!’\nلَعَلَّنَا نَتَّبِعُ السَّحَرَةَ اِنْ كَانُوْا هُمُ الْغٰلِبِيْنَ‏(40)\nLA-A’LLANAA NATTABE-U’S SAHARATA IN KAANOO HOMUL GHAALEBEEN.\n‘Maybe we will follow the magicians, if they are victors!’\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ السَّحَرَةُ قَالُوْا لِفِرْعَوْنَ اَئِنَّ لَنَا لَاَجْرًا اِنْ كُنَّا نَحْنُ الْغٰلِبِيْنَ‏(41)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AS SAHARATO QAALOO LE-FIR-A’WNA A-INNA LANAA LA-AJRAN IN KUNNAA NAHNUL GHAALEBEEN.\nSo when the magicians came, they said to Pharaoh, ‘Shall we have a reward if we were to be the victors?’\nقَالَ نَعَمْ وَاِنَّكُمْ اِذًا لَّمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ‏(42)\nQAALA NA-A’M WA INNAKUM EZAL LAMENAL MOQARRABEEN.\nHe said, ‘Of course; and you will be among members of my inner circle.’\nقَالَ لَهُمْ مُّوْسٰۤى اَلْقُوْا مَاۤ اَنْتُمْ مُّلْقُوْنَ‏(43)\nQAALA LAHUM MOOSAA ALQOO MAA ANTUM MULQOON.\nMoses said to them, ‘Throw down whatever you have to throw!’\nفَاَلْقَوْا حِبَالَهُمْ وَعِصِيَّهُمْ وَقَالُوْا بِعِزَّةِ فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّا لَنَحْنُ الْغٰلِبُوْنَ‏(44)\nFA-ALQAW HEBAALAHUM WA E’SIYYAHUM WA QAALOO BE-I’ZZATE FIR-A’WNA INNAA LANAHNUL GHAALEBOON.\nSo they threw down their sticks and ropes, and said, ‘By the might of Pharaoh, we shall surely be victorious!’\nفَاَ لْقٰى مُوْسٰى عَصَاهُ فَاِذَا هِىَ تَلْقَفُ مَا يَاْفِكُوْنَ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(45)\nFA-ALQAA MOOSAA A’SAAHO FA-EZAA HEYA TALQAFO MAA YAAFEKOON.\nThereat Moses threw down his staff, and behold, it was swallowing what they had faked.\nفَاُلْقِىَ السَّحَرَةُ سٰجِدِيْنَۙ‏(46)\nFA-ULQEYAS SAHARATO SAAJEDEEN.\nThereat the magicians fell down prostrating.\nقَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(47)\nQAALOO AAMANNAA BE-RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nThey said, ‘We believe in the Lord of all the worlds,\nرَبِّ مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ‏(48)\nRABBE MOOSAA WA HAAROON.\nthe Lord of Moses and Aaron.’\nقَالَ اٰمَنْتُمْ لَهٗ قَبْلَ اَنْ اٰذَنَ لَكُمْ‌ۚ اِنَّهٗ لَكَبِيْرُكُمُ الَّذِىْ عَلَّمَكُمُ السِّحْرَ‌ۚ فَلَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَ ۙ لَاُقَطِّعَنَّ اَيْدِيَكُمْ وَاَرْجُلَكُمْ مِّنْ خِلَافٍ وَّلَاُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(49)\nQAALA AAMANTUM LAHU QABLA AN AAZANA LAKUM, INNAHU LA-KABEEROKOMUL LAZEE A’LLAMAKOMUS SEHR, FALASAWFA TA’LAMOONA, LA-OQATTE-A’NNA AYDEYAKUM WA ARJOLAKUM MIN KHELAAFINW WA LA-OSALLEBANNAKUM AJMA-E’EN.\nHe [i.e. Pharaoh] said, ‘Do you profess faith in Him before I should permit you? He is indeed your chief who has taught you magic! Soon you will know! I will cut off your hands and feet from opposite sides, and I will crucify you all.’\nقَالُوْا لَا ضَيْرَ‌ اِنَّاۤ اِلٰى رَبِّنَا مُنْقَلِبُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(50)\nQAALOO LAA ZAYR, INNAA ELAA RABBENAA MUNQALEBOON.\nThey said, ‘[There is] no harm [in that]! Indeed, we shall return to our Lord.\nاِنَّا نَطْمَعُ اَنْ يَّغْفِرَ لَنَا رَبُّنَا خَطٰيٰنَاۤ اَنْ كُنَّاۤ اَوَّلَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَؕ‏(51)\nINNAA NATMA-O’ AN-Y YAGHFERA LANAA RABBONAA KHATAAYAANAA AN KUNNAA AWWALAL MOAMENEEN.\nIndeed we hope our Lord will forgive us our offences for being the first to believe.’\nوَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى اَنْ اَسْرِ بِعِبَادِىْۤ اِنَّكُمْ مُّتَّبَعُوْنَ‏(52)\nWA AWHAYNAA ELAA MOOSAA AN ASRE BE-E’BAADEE INNAKUM MUTTABA-O’ON.\nThen We revealed to Moses, [saying],‘Set out with My servants at night, for you will be pursued.’\nفَاَرْسَلَ فِرْعَوْنُ فِى الْمَدَآئِنِ حٰشِرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(53)\nFA-ARSALA FIR-A’WNO FIL MADAAA-ENE HAASHEREEN.\nThen Pharaoh sent heralds to the cities,\nاِنَّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ لَشِرْذِمَةٌ قَلِيْلُوْنَۙ‏(54)\nINNA HAA-OLAAA-E LA-SHIRZEMATUN QALEELOON.\n[proclaiming:] ‘These are indeed a small band.\nوَاِنَّهُمْ لَنَا لَغَآئِظُوْنَۙ‏(55)\nWA INNAHUM LANAA LA-GHAAA-EZOON.\nThey have aroused our wrath,\nوَاِنَّا لَجَمِيْعٌ حٰذِرُوْنَؕ‏(56)\nWA INNAA LA-JAMEE-U’N HAAZEROON.\nand we are alert and fully prepared.’\nفَاَخْرَجْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(57)\nFA-AKHRAJNAAHUM MIN JANNAATINW WA O’YOON.\nSo We took them out of gardens and springs,\nوَّكُنُوْزٍ وَّمَقَامٍ كَرِيْمٍۙ‏(58)\nWA KONOOZINW WA MAQAAMIN KAREEM.\nand [made them leave behind] treasures and stately homes.\nكَذٰلِكَؕ وَاَوْرَثْنٰهَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَؕ‏(59)\nKAZAALEK, WA AWRASNAAHAA BANEE ISRAAA-EEL.\nSo it was; and We bequeathed them to the Children of Israel.\nفَاَ تْبَعُوْهُمْ مُّشْرِقِيْنَ‏(60)\nFA-ATBA-O’OHUM MUSHREQEEN.\nThen they pursued them at sunrise.\nفَلَمَّا تَرَآءَ الْجَمْعٰنِ قَالَ اَصْحٰبُ مُوْسٰٓى اِنَّا لَمُدْرَكُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(61)\nFALAMMAA TARAAA-AL JAM-A’ANE QAALA ASHAABO MOOSAA INNAA LA-MUDRAKOON.\nWhen the two hosts sighted each other, the companions of Moses said, ‘Indeed we have been caught up.’\nقَالَ كَلَّا‌‌ ۚ اِنَّ مَعِىَ رَبِّىْ سَيَهْدِيْنِ‏(62)\nQAALA KALLAA, INNA MA-E’YA RABBEE SAYAHDEEN.\nHe said, ‘Certainly not! Indeed my Lord is with me. He will guide me.’\nفَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى اَنِ اضْرِبْ بِّعَصَاكَ الْبَحْرَ‌ؕ فَانْفَلَقَ فَكَانَ كُلُّ فِرْقٍ كَالطَّوْدِ الْعَظِيْمِ‌ۚ‏(63)\nFA-AWHAYNAA ELAA MOOSAA ANIZ RIB BE-A’SAAKAL BAHR, FANFALAQA FA-KAANA KULLO FIRQIN KAT-TAWDIL A’ZEEM.\nThereupon We revealed to Moses: ‘Strike the sea with your staff!’ Whereupon it parted, and each part was as if it were a great mountain.\nوَاَزْلَفْنَا ثَمَّ الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(64)\nWA AZLAFNAA SAMMAL AAKHAREEN.\nThere, We brought the others near,\nوَاَنْجَيْنَا مُوْسٰى وَمَنْ مَّعَهٗۤ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(65)\nWA ANJAYNAA MOOSAA WA MAM MA-A’HU AJMA-E’EN.\nand We delivered Moses and all those who were with him.\nثُمَّ اَغْرَقْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‌ؕ‏(66)\nSUMMA AGHRAQNAL AAKHAREEN.\nThen We drowned the rest.\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاَيَةً ‌ ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(67)\nINNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAH, WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nThere is indeed a sign in that, but most of them do not have faith.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(68)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUR RAHEEM.\nIndeed your Lord is the All-mighty, the All-merciful.\nوَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَاَ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ‌ۘ‏(69)\nWAT LO A’LAYHIM NABA-A IBRAAHEEM.\nRelate to them the account of Abraham\nاِذْ قَالَ لِاَبِيْهِ وَقَوْمِهٖ مَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(70)\nIZ QAALA LE-ABEEHE WA QAWMEHI MAA TA’BODOON.\nwhen he said to his father and his people, ‘What is it that you are worshiping?!’\nقَالُوْا نَعْبُدُ اَصْنَامًا فَنَظَلُّ لَهَا عٰكِفِيْنَ‏(71)\nQAALOO NA’BODO ASNAAMAN FA-NAZALLO LAHAA A’AKEFEEN.\nThey said, ‘We worship idols, and are constant in our devotion to them.’\nقَالَ هَلْ يَسْمَعُوْنَكُمْ اِذْ تَدْعُوْنَۙ‏(72)\nQAALA HAL YASMA-O’ONAKUM IZ TAD-O’ON.\nHe said, ‘Do they hear you when you call them?\nاَوْ يَنْفَعُوْنَكُمْ اَوْ يَضُرُّوْنَ‏(73)\nAW YANFA-O’ONAKUM AW YAZURROON.\nOr do they bring you any benefit, or cause you any harm?’\nقَالُوْا بَلْ وَجَدْنَاۤ اٰبَآءَنَا كَذٰلِكَ يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(74)\nQAALOO BAL WAJADNAA AABAAA-ANAA KAZAALEKA YAF-A’LOON.\nThey said, ‘Indeed, we found our fathers doing likewise.’\nقَالَ اَفَرَءَيْتُمْ مَّا كُنْتُمْ تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(75)\nQAALA AFA-RA-AYTUM MAA KUNTUM TA’BODOON.\nHe said, ‘Have you regarded what you have been worshipping,\nاَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَآؤُكُمُ الْاَقْدَمُوْنَ ‌ۖ ‏(76)\nANTUM WA AABAAA-OKOMUL AQDAMOON.\nyou and your ancestors?\nفَاِنَّهُمْ عَدُوٌّ لِّىْۤ اِلَّا رَبَّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(77)\nFA-INNAHUM A’DUWWUL LEE ILLAA RABBAL A’ALAMEEN.\nThey are indeed enemies to me, but the Lord of all the worlds,\nالَّذِىْ خَلَقَنِىْ فَهُوَ يَهْدِيْنِۙ‏(78)\nLAZEE KHALAQANEE FAHOWA YAHDEEN.\nwho created me, it is He who guides me,\nوَ الَّذِىْ هُوَ يُطْعِمُنِىْ وَيَسْقِيْنِۙ‏(79)\nWAL LAZEE HOWA YUT-E’MONEE WA YASQEEN.\nand provides me with food and drink,\nوَاِذَا مَرِضْتُ فَهُوَ يَشْفِيْنِ ۙ‏(80)\nWA EZAA MARIZTO FAHOWA YASHFEEN.\nand when I get sick, it is He who cures me;\nوَالَّذِىْ يُمِيْتُنِىْ ثُمَّ يُحْيِيْنِۙ‏(81)\nWAL LAZEE YOMEETONEE SUMMA YOHYEEN.\nwho will make me die, then He will bring me to life,\nوَالَّذِىْۤ اَطْمَعُ اَنْ يَّغْفِرَ لِىْ خَطِٓیْئَتِىْ يَوْمَ الدِّيْنِ ؕ‏(82)\nWAL LAZEE ATMA-O’ AN-Y YAGHFERA LEE KHATEE-ATEE YAWMAD DEEN.\nand who, I hope, will forgive me my faults on the Day of Retribution.’\nرَبِّ هَبْ لِىْ حُكْمًا وَّاَلْحِقْنِىْ بِالصّٰلِحِيْنَۙ‏(83)\nRABBE HAB LEE HUKMANW WA ALHIQNEE BIS-SAALEHEEN.\n‘My Lord! Grant me [unerring] judgement, and unite me with the Righteous.\nوَاجْعَلْ لِّىْ لِسَانَ صِدْقٍ فِى الْاٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(84)\nWAJ A’L LEE LESAANA SIDQIN FIL AAKHEREEN.\nConfer on me a worthy repute among the posterity,\nوَاجْعَلْنِىْ مِنْ وَّرَثَةِ جَنَّةِ النَّعِيْمِۙ‏(85)\nWAJ A’LNEE MINW WARASATE JANNATIN NA-E’EM.\nand make me one of the heirs to the paradise of bliss.\nوَاغْفِرْ لِاَبِىْۤ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ مِنَ الضَّآلِّيْنَۙ‏(86)\nWAGH FIR LE-ABEE INNAHU KAANA MENAZ ZAALLEEN.\nForgive my father, for he is one of those who are astray.\nوَلَا تُخْزِنِىْ يَوْمَ يُبْعَثُوْنَۙ‏(87)\nWA LAA TUKHZENEE YAWMA YUB-A’SOON.\nDo not disgrace me on the day that they will be resurrected,\nيَوْمَ لَا يَنْفَعُ مَالٌ وَّلَا بَنُوْنَۙ‏(88)\nYAWMA LAA YANFA-O’ MAALUNW WA LAA BANOON.\nthe day when neither wealth nor children will avail,\nاِلَّا مَنْ اَتَى اللّٰهَ بِقَلْبٍ سَلِيْمٍؕ‏(89)\nILLAA MAN ATAL LAAHA BE-QALBIN SALEEM.\nexcept him who comes to Allah with a sound heart,’\nوَاُزْلِفَتِ الْجَنَّةُ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(90)\nWA UZLEFATIL JANNATO LIL-MUTTAQEEN.\nand paradise will be brought near for the Godwary,\nوَبُرِّزَتِ الْجَحِيْمُ لِلْغٰوِيْنَۙ‏(91)\nWA BURREZATIL JAHEEMO LIL-GHAAWEEN.\nand hell will be brought into view for the perverse,\nوَقِيْلَ لَهُمْ اَيْنَمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(92)\nWA QEELA LAHUM AYNA MAA KUNTUM TA’BODOON.\nand they shall be told: ‘Where is that which you used to worship\nمِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِؕ هَلْ يَنْصُرُوْنَكُمْ اَوْ يَنْتَصِرُوْنَؕ‏(93)\nMIN DOONIL LAAH, HAL YANSOROONAKUM AW YANTASEROON.\nbesides Allah? Do they help you, or do they help each other?’\nفَكُبْكِبُوْا فِيْهَا هُمْ وَالْغَاوٗنَۙ‏(94)\nFA-KUBKEBOO FEEHAA HUM WAL GHAAWOON.\nThen they will be cast into it on their faces—they and the perverse,\nوَجُنُوْدُ اِبْلِيْسَ اَجْمَعُوْنَؕ‏(95)\nWA JONOODO IBLEESA AJMA-O’ON.\nand the hosts of Iblis all together.\nقَالُوْا وَهُمْ فِيْهَا يَخْتَصِمُوْنَۙ‏(96)\nQAALOO WA HUM FEEHAA YAKHTASEMOON.\nThey will say, as they wrangle in it [together],\nتَاللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنَّا لَفِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(97)\nTALLAAHE IN KUNNAA LAFEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\n‘By Allah, we had indeed been in manifest error\nاِذْ نُسَوِّيْكُمْ بِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(98)\nIZ NOSAWWEEKUM BE-RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nwhen we equated you with the Lord of all the worlds!\nوَمَاۤ اَضَلَّنَاۤ اِلَّا الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(99)\nWA MAA AZALLANAA ILLAL MUJREMOON.\nNo one led us astray except the guilty.\nفَمَا لَنَا مِنْ شٰفِعِيْنَۙ‏(100)\nFAMAA LANAA MIN SHAAFE-E’EN.\nNow we have no intercessors,\nوَلَا صَدِيْقٍ حَمِيْمٍ‏(101)\nWA LAA SADEEQIN HAMEEM.\nnor do we have any sympathetic friend.\nفَلَوْ اَنَّ لَنَا كَرَّةً فَنَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(102)\nFALAW ANNA LANAA KARRATAN FA-NAKOONA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nHad there been another turn for us, we would be among the faithful.’\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً‌  ؕ وَّمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(103)\nINNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAH, WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nThere is indeed a sign in that; but most of them do not have faith.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(104)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUR RAHEEM.\nIndeed your Lord is the All-mighty, the All-merciful.\nكَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ نُوْحِۨالْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(105)\nKAZZABAT QAWMO NOOHENIL MURSALEEN.\nThe people of Noah impugned the apostles\nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ اَخُوْهُمْ نُوْحٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(106)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM AKHOOHUM NOOHUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nwhen Noah, their brother, said to them, ‘Will you not be wary [of Allah]?\nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(107)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUN AMEEN.\nIndeed I am a trusted apostle [sent] to you.\nفَاتَّقُوْا اللّٰهَ وَ اَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(108)\nFAT-TAQUL LAAHA WA ATEE-O’ON.\nSo be wary of Allah and obey me.\nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(109)\nWA MAA AS-ALOKUM A’LAYHE MIN AJR, IN AJREYA ILLAA A’LAA RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nI do not ask you any reward for it; my reward lies only with the Lord of all the worlds.\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ ؕ‏(110)\nFAT-TAQUL LAAHA WA ATEE-O’ON.\nSo be wary of Allah and obey me.’\nقَالُوْۤا اَنُؤْمِنُ لَكَ وَاتَّبَعَكَ الْاَرْذَلُوْنَؕ‏(111)\nQAALOO ANOAMENO LAKA WAT TABA-A’KAL ARZALOON.\nThey said, ‘Shall we believe in you, when it is the riffraff who follow you?’\nقَالَ وَمَا عِلْمِىْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(112)\nQAALA WA MAA I’LMEE BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nHe said, ‘What do I know as to what they used to do?\nاِنْ حِسَابُهُمْ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّىْ‌ لَوْ تَشْعُرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(113)\nIN HESAABOHUM ILLAA A’LAA RABBEE LAW TASH-O’ROON.\nTheir reckoning is only with my Lord, should you be aware.\nوَمَاۤ اَنَا بِطَارِدِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(114)\nWA MAA ANAA BE-TAAREDIL MOAMENEEN.\nI will not drive away the faithful.\nاِنْ اَنَا اِلَّا نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌؕ‏(115)\nIN ANAA ILLAA NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nI am just a manifest warner.’\nقَالُوْا لَئِنْ لَّمْ تَنْتَهِ يٰنُوْحُ لَتَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمَرْجُوْمِيْنَؕ‏(116)\nQAALOO LA-IL LAM TANTAHE YAA NOOHO LATAKOONANNA MENAL MARJOOMEEN.\nThey said, ‘Noah, if you do not desist, you will certainly be stoned [to death].’\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنَّ قَوْمِىْ كَذَّبُوْنِ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(117)\nQAALA RABBE INNA QAWMEE KAZZABOON.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! Indeed my people have impugned me.\nفَافْتَحْ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَهُمْ فَتْحًا وَّنَجِّنِىْ وَمَنْ مَّعِىَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(118)\nFAFTAH BAYNEE WA BAYNAHUM FATHANW WA NAJJENEE WA MAM MA-E’YA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nSo judge conclusively between me and them, and deliver me and the faithful who are with me.’\nفَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَمَنْ مَّعَهٗ فِى الْفُلْكِ الْمَشْحُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(119)\nFA-ANJAYNAAHO WA MAM MA-A’HU FIL FULKIL MASH-HOON.\nThereupon We delivered him and those who were with him in the laden ark.\nثُمَّ اَغْرَقْنَا بَعْدُ الْبٰقِيْنَؕ‏(120)\nSUMMA AGHRAQNAA BA’DUL BAAQEEN.\nThen We drowned the rest.\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاَيَةً‌  ؕ وَّمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(121)\nINNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAH, WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nThere is indeed a sign in that; but most of them do not have faith.\nوَ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(122)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUR RAHEEM.\nIndeed your Lord is the All-mighty, the All-merciful.\nكَذَّبَتْ عَادُ اۨلْمُرْسَلِيْنَ ‌ۖ ‌ۚ‏(123)\nKAZZABAT A’ADONIL MURSALEEN.\n[The people of] ‘Ad impugned the apostles,\nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ اَخُوْهُمْ هُوْدٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(124)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM AKHOOHUM HOODUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nwhen Hud, their brother, said to them, ‘Will you not be wary [of Allah]?\nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌ‌ۙ‏(125)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUN AMEEN.\nIndeed I am a trusted apostle [sent] to you.\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ ۚ‏(126)\nFAT-TAQUL LAAHA WA ATEE-O’ON.\nSo be wary of Allah and obey me.\nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ؕ‏(127)\nWA MAA AS-ALOKUM A’LAYHE MIN AJR, IN AJREYA ILLAA A’LAA RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nI do not ask you any reward for it; my reward lies only with the Lord of all the worlds.\nاَتَبْنُوْنَ بِكُلِّ رِيْعٍ اٰيَةً تَعْبَثُوْنَۙ‏(128)\nATABNOONA BE-KULLE REE-I’N AAYATAN TA’BASOON.\nDo you build futile a sign on every prominence?\nوَ تَتَّخِذُوْنَ مَصَانِعَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَخْلُدُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(129)\nWA TATTAKHEZOONA MASAANE-A’ LA-A’LLAKUM TAKHLODOON.\nYou set up structures as if you will be immortal,\nوَاِذَا بَطَشْتُمْ بَطَشْتُمْ جَبَّارِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(130)\nWA EZAA BATASHTUM BATASHTUM JABBAAREEN.\nand when you seize [someone for punishment], you seize [him] like tyrants.\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ ۚ‏(131)\nFAT-TAQUL LAAHA WA ATEE-O’ON.\nSo be wary of Allah and obey me.\nوَاتَّقُوْا الَّذِىْۤ اَمَدَّكُمْ بِمَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(132)\nWAT TAQUL LAZEE AMADDAKUM BEMAA TA’LAMOON.\nBe wary of Him who has provided you with whatever you know,\nاَمَدَّكُمْ بِاَنْعَامٍ وَّبَنِيْنَ ‌ۚۙ‏(133)\nAMADDAKUM BE-AN-A’AMINW WA BANEEN.\nand aided you with sons and with cattle,\nوَجَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍ‌ۚ‏(134)\nWA JANNAATINW WA O’YOON.\ngardens and springs.\nاِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍؕ‏(135)\nINNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABA YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nIndeed I fear for you the punishment of a tremendous day.’\nقَالُوْا سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْنَاۤ اَوَعَظْتَ اَمْ لَمْ تَكُنْ مِّنَ الْوٰعِظِيْنَۙ‏(136)\nQAALOO SAWAAA-UN A’LAYNAA AWA-A’ZTA AM LAM TAKUM MENAL WAA-E’ZEEN.\nThey said, ‘It is the same to us whether you exhort us or not.\nاِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا خُلُقُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَۙ‏(137)\nIN HAAZAA ILLAA KHOLOQUL AWWALEEN.\nThese are nothing but the traditions of the ancients,\nوَمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(138)\nWA MAA NAHNO BE-MO-A’ZZABEEN.\nand we will not be punished.’\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَاَيَةً‌ ؕ وَ مَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(139)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FA-AHLAKNAAHUM, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAH, WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nSo they impugned him, whereupon We destroyed them. There is indeed a sign in that; but most of them do not have faith.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(140)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUR RAHEEM.\nIndeed your Lord is the All-mighty, the All-merciful.\nكَذَّبَتْ ثَمُوْدُ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‌ ۖ‌ۚ‏(141)\nKAZZABAT SAMOODUL MURSALEEN.\n[The people of] Thamud impugned the apostles\nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ اَخُوْهُمْ صٰلِحٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(142)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM AKHOOHUM SAALEHUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nwhen Salih, their brother, said to them, ‘Will you not be wary [of Allah]?\nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(143)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUN AMEEN.\nIndeed I am a trusted apostle [sent] to you.\nفَاتَّقُوْا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(144)\nFAT-TAQUL LAAHA WA ATEE-O’ON.\nSo be wary of Allah and obey me.\nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(145)\nWA MAA AS-ALOKUM A’LAYHE MIN AJR, IN AJREYA ILLAA A’LAA RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nI do not ask you any reward for it; my reward lies only with the Lord of all the worlds.\nاَتُتْرَكُوْنَ فِىْ مَا هٰهُنَاۤ اٰمِنِيْنَۙ‏(146)\nATUTRAKOONA FEE MAA HAAHONAA AAMENEEN.\nWill you be left secure in that which is here\nفِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(147)\nFEE JANNAATINW WA O’YOON.\n—amid gardens and springs,\nوَّزُرُوْعٍ وَّنَخْلٍ طَلْعُهَا هَضِيْمٌ‌ۚ‏(148)\nWA ZOROO-I’NW WA NAKHLIN TAL-O’HAA HAZEEM.\nfarms and date palms with dainty spathes\nوَتَنْحِتُوْنَ مِنَ الْجِبَالِ بُيُوْتًا فٰرِهِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(149)\nWA TANHETOONA MENAL JEBAALE BOYOOTAN FAAREHEEN.\n—while you skillfully hew out houses from the mountains?\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ ۚ‏(150)\nFAT-TAQUL LAAHA WA ATEE-O’ON.\nSo be wary of Allah and obey me,\nوَلَا تُطِيْعُوْۤا اَمْرَ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَۙ‏(151)\nWA LAA TOTEE-O’O AMRAL MUSREFEEN.\nand do not obey the dictates of the transgressors,\nالَّذِيْنَ يُفْسِدُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَ لَا يُصْلِحُوْنَ‏(152)\nLAZEENA YUFSEDOONA FIL ARZE WA LAA YUSLEHOON.\nwho cause corruption in the land and do not bring about reform.’\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مِنَ الْمُسَحَّرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(153)\nQAALOO INNAMAA ANTA MENAL MOSAHHAREEN.\nThey said, ‘Indeed you are one of the bewitched.\nمَاۤ اَنْتَ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَا ‌ ۖۚ فَاْتِ بِاٰيَةٍ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(154)\nMAA ANTA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLONAA, FAATE BE-AAYATIN IN KUNTA MENAS SAADEQEEN.\nYou are just a human being like us. So bring us a sign, should you be truthful.’\nقَالَ هٰذِهٖ نَاقَةٌ لَّهَا شِرْبٌ وَّلَكُمْ شِرْبُ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُوْمٍ‌ۚ‏(155)\nQAALA HAAZEHI NAAQATUL LAHAA SHIRBUNW WA LAKUM SHIRBO YAWMIM MA’LOOM.\nHe said, ‘This is a she-camel; she shall drink and you shall drink on known days.\nوَلَا تَمَسُّوْهَا بِسُوْٓءٍ فَيَاْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(156)\nWA LAA TAMASSOOHAA BE-SOO-IN FA-YAAKHOZAKUM A’ZAABO YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nDo not cause her any harm, for then you shall be seized by the punishment of a terrible day.’\nفَعَقَرُوْهَا فَاَصْبَحُوْا نٰدِمِيْنَۙ‏(157)\nFA-A’QAROOHAA FA-ASBAHOO NAADEMEEN.\nBut they hamstrung her, whereupon they became regretful.\nفَاَخَذَهُمُ الْعَذَابُ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً‌  ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(158)\nFA-AKHAZAHOMUL A’ZAAB, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAH, WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nSo the punishment seized them. There is indeed a sign in that; but most of them do not have faith.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(159)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUR RAHEEM.\nIndeed your Lord is the All-mighty, the All-merciful.\nكَذَّبَتْ قَوْمُ لُوْطٍ اۨلْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(160)\nKAZZABAT QAWMO LOOTENIL MURSALEEN.\nThe people of Lot impugned the apostles\nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ اَخُوْهُمْ لُوْطٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(161)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM AKHOOHUM LOOTUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nwhen Lot, their brother, said to them, ‘Will you not be wary [of Allah]?\nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(162)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUN AMEEN.\nIndeed I am a trusted apostle [sent] to you.\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(163)\nFAT-TAQUL LAAHA WA ATEE-O’ON.\nSo be wary of Allah and obey me.\nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ؕ‏(164)\nWA MAA AS-ALOKUM A’LAYHE MIN AJR, IN AJREYA ILLAA A’LAA RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nI do not ask you any reward for it; my reward lies only with the Lord of all the worlds.\nاَتَاْتُوْنَ الذُّكْرَانَ مِنَ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(165)\nATAATOONAZ ZUKRAANA MENAL A’ALAMEEN.\nWhat! Of all people do you come to males,\nوَ تَذَرُوْنَ مَا خَلَقَ لَكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ مِّنْ اَزْوَاجِكُمْ‌ؕ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ عٰدُوْنَ‏(166)\nWA TAZAROONA MAA KHALAQA LAKUM RABBOKUM MIN AZWAAJEKUM, BAL ANTUM QAWMUN A’ADOON.\nabandoning your wives your Lord has created for you? Indeed, you are a transgressing lot.’\nقَالُوْا لَئِنْ لَّمْ تَنْتَهِ يٰلُوْطُ لَتَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْمُخْرَجِيْنَ‏(167)\nQAALOO LA-IL LAM TANTAHE YAA LOOTO LATAKOONANNA MENAL MUKHRAJEEN.\nThey said, ‘Lot, if you do not desist, you will surely be banished.’\nقَالَ اِنِّىْ لِعَمَلِكُمْ مِّنَ الْقَالِيْنَؕ‏(168)\nQAALA INNEE LE-A’MALEKUM MENAL QAALEEN.\nHe said, ‘Indeed I detest your conduct.’\nرَبِّ نَجِّنِىْ وَاَهْلِىْ مِمَّا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(169)\nRABBE NAJJENEE WA AHLEE MIMMAA YA’MALOON.\n‘My Lord! Deliver me and my family from what they do.’\nفَنَجَّيْنٰهُ وَ اَهْلَهٗۤ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(170)\nFA-NAJJAYNAAHO WA AHLAHU AJMA-E’EN.\nSo We delivered him and all his family,\nاِلَّا عَجُوْزًا فِى الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(171)\nILLAA A’JOOZAN FIL GHAABEREEN.\nexcept an old woman who remained behind.\nثُمَّ دَمَّرْنَا الْاٰخَرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(172)\nSUMMA DAMMARNAL AAKHAREEN.\nThen We destroyed [all] the rest,\nوَاَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مَّطَرًا‌ۚ فَسَآءَ مَطَرُ الْمُنْذَرِيْنَ‏(173)\nWA AMTARNAA A’LAYHIM MATARAA, FA-SAAA-A MATARUL MUNZAREEN.\nand rained down upon them a rain [of stones]. Evil was the rain of those who were warned!\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاَيَةً‌  ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(174)\nINNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAH, WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nThere is indeed a sign in that; but most of them do not have faith.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(175)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUR RAHEEM.\nIndeed your Lord is the All-mighty, the All-merciful.\nكَذَّبَ اَصْحٰبُ لْئَيْكَةِ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ ‌ۖ‌ۚ‏(176)\nKAZZABA ASHAABUL AYKATIL MURSALEEN.\nThe inhabitants of Aykah impugned the apostles,\nاِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ شُعَيْبٌ اَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(177)\nIZ QAALA LAHUM SHO-A’YBUN ALAA TATTAQOON.\nwhen Shu‘ayb said to them, ‘Will you not be wary [of Allah]?\nاِنِّىْ لَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ اَمِيْنٌۙ‏(178)\nINNEE LAKUM RASOOLUN AMEEN.\nIndeed I am a trusted apostle [sent] to you.\nفَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‌ۚ‏(179)\nFAT-TAQUL LAAHA WA ATEE-O’ON.\nSo be wary of Allah and obey me.\nوَمَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ اَجْرٍ‌ۚ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلٰى رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ؕ‏(180)\nWA MAA AS-ALOKUM A’LAYHE MIN AJR, IN AJREYA ILLAA A’LAA RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nI do not ask you any reward for it; my reward lies only with the Lord of all the worlds.\nاَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ وَلَا تَكُوْنُوْا مِنَ الْمُخْسِرِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(181)\nAWFUL KAYLA WA LAA TAKOONOO MENAL MUKHSEREEN.\nObserve the full measure, and do not be of those who give short measure.\nوَزِنُوْا بِالْقِسْطَاسِ الْمُسْتَقِيْمِ‌ۚ‏(182)\nWA ZENOO BIL-QISTAASIL MUSTAQEEM.\nWeigh with an even balance,\nوَلَا تَبْخَسُوا النَّاسَ اَشْيَآءَهُمْ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ مُفْسِدِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(183)\nWA LAA TABKHASUN NAASA ASHYAAA-AHUM WA LAA TA’SAW FIL ARZE MUFSEDEEN.\nand do not cheat the people of their goods. Do not act wickedly on the earth, causing corruption.\nوَاتَّقُوا الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ وَالْجِبِلَّةَ الْاَوَّلِيْنَؕ‏(184)\nWAT TAQUL LAZEE KHALAQAKUM WAL JEBILLATAL AWWALEEN.\nBe wary of Him who created you and the earlier generations.’\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مِنَ الْمُسَحَّرِيْنَۙ‏(185)\nQAALOO INNAMAA ANTA MENAL MOSAHHAREEN.\nThey said, ‘Indeed you are one of the bewitched.\nوَمَاۤ اَنْتَ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَا وَ اِنْ نَّظُنُّكَ لَمِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(186)\nWA MAA ANTA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLONAA WA IN NAZUNNOKA LAMENAL KAAZEBEEN.\nYou are just a human being like us, and we indeed consider you to be a liar.\nفَاَسْقِطْ عَلَيْنَا كِسَفًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَؕ‏(187)\nFA-ASQIT A’LAYNAA KESAFAM MENAS SAMAAA-E IN KUNTA MENAS SAADEQEEN.\nMake a fragment of the sky falls upon us, should you be truthful.’\nقَالَ رَبِّىْۤ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(188)\nQAALA RABBEE A-A’LAMO BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nHe said, ‘My Lord knows best what you are doing.’\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاَخَذَهُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمِ الظُّلَّةِ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ كَانَ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(189)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FA-AKHAZAHUM A’ZAABO YAWMIZ ZULLAH, INNAHU KAANA A’ZAABA YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nSo they impugned him, and then they were overtaken by the punishment of the day of the overshadowing cloud. It was indeed the punishment of a terrible day.\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاَيَةً ‌ ؕ وَمَا كَانَ اَكْثَرُهُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(190)\nINNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAH, WA MAA KAANA AKSAROHUM MOAMENEEN.\nThere is indeed a sign in that; but most of them do not have faith.\nوَاِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(191)\nWA INNA RABBAKA LAHOWAL A’ZEEZUR RAHEEM.\nIndeed your Lord is the All-mighty, the All-merciful.\nوَاِنَّهٗ لَتَنْزِيْلُ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَؕ‏(192)\nWA INNAHU LA-TANZEELO RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nThis is indeed [a Book] sent down by the Lord of all the worlds,\nنَزَلَ بِهِ الرُّوْحُ الْاَمِيْنُۙ‏(193)\nNAZALA BEHIR ROOHUL AMEEN.\nbrought down by the Trustworthy Spirit\nعَلٰى قَلْبِكَ لِتَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُنْذِرِيْنَۙ‏(194)\nA’LAA QALBEKA LE-TAKOONA MENAL MUNZEREEN.\nupon your heart (so that you may be one of the warners),\nبِلِسَانٍ عَرَبِىٍّ مُّبِيْنٍؕ‏(195)\nBE-LESAANIN A’RABIYYIM MOBEEN.\nin a clear Arabic language.\nوَاِنَّهٗ لَفِىْ زُبُرِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(196)\nWA INNAHU LAFEE ZOBORIL AWWALEEN.\nIt is indeed [foretold] in the scriptures of the ancients.\nاَوَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهُمْ اٰيَةً اَنْ يَّعْلَمَهٗ عُلَمٰٓؤُا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَؕ‏(197)\nAWA LAM YAKUL LAHUM AAYATAN AN-Y YA’LAMAHU O’LAMAAA-O BANEE ISRAAA-EEL.\nIs it not a sign for them that the learned of the Children of Israel recognize it?\nوَلَوْ نَزَّلْنٰهُ عَلٰى بَعْضِ الْاَعْجَمِيْنَۙ‏(198)\nWA LAW NAZZALNAAHO A’LAA BA’ZIL A-A’JAMEEN.\nHad We sent it down upon some non-Arab\nفَقَرَاَهٗ عَلَيْهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ مُؤْمِنِيْنَؕ‏(199)\nFA-QARA-AHU A’LAYHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI MOAMENEEN.\nand had he recited it to them, they would not have believed in it.\nكَذٰلِكَ سَلَكْنٰهُ فِىْ قُلُوْبِ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَؕ‏(200)\nKAZAALEKA SALAKNAAHO FEE QOLOOBIL MUJREMEEN.\nThis is how We let it pass through the hearts of the guilty:\nلَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ حَتّٰى يَرَوُا الْعَذَابَ الْاَلِيْمَۙ‏(201)\nLAA YOAMENOONA BEHI HATTAA YARAWUL A’ZAABAL ALEEM.\nthey do not believe in it until they sight the painful punishment.\nفَيَاْتِيَهُمْ بَغْتَةً وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَۙ‏(202)\nFA-YAATEYAHUM BAGHTATANW WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nIt will overtake them suddenly while they are unaware.\nفَيَقُوْلُوْا هَلْ نَحْنُ مُنْظَرُوْنَؕ‏(203)\nFA-YAQOOLOO HAL NAHNO MUNZAROON.\nThereupon they will say, ‘Shall we be granted any respite?’\nاَفَبِعَذَابِنَا يَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَ‏(204)\nAFABE-A’ZAABENAA YASTA’JELOON.\nSo do they seek to hasten on Our punishment?\nاَفَرَءَيْتَ اِنْ مَّتَّعْنٰهُمْ سِنِيْنَۙ‏(205)\nAFA-RA-AYTA IM MATTA’NAAHUM SENEEN.\nTell me, should We let them enjoy for some years,\nثُمَّ جَآءَهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يُوْعَدُوْنَۙ‏(206)\nSUMMA JAAA-AHUM MAA KAANOO YOO-A’DOON.\nthen there comes to them what they have been promised,\nمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يُمَتَّعُوْنَؕ‏(207)\nMAA AGHNAA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YOMATTA-O’ON.\nof what avail to them will be that which they were given to enjoy?\nوَمَاۤ اَهْلَكْنَا مِنْ قَرْيَةٍ اِلَّا لَهَا مُنْذِرُوْنَ‌‌‌‌‌ ۛ ‌ۖ ‏(208)\nWA MAA AHLAKNAA MIN QARYATIN ILLAA LAHAA MUNZEROON.\nWe have not destroyed any town without its having warners,\nذِكْرٰى‌ۛ وَمَا كُنَّا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(209)\nZIKRAA, WA MAA KUNNAA ZAALEMEEN.\nfor the sake of admonition, and We were not unjust.\nوَمَا تَنَزَّلَتْ بِهِ الشَّيٰطِيْنُ‏(210)\nWA MAA TANAZZALAT BEHISH SHAYAATEEN.\nIt has not been brought down by the devils.\nوَمَا يَنْۢبَغِىْ لَهُمْ وَمَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَؕ‏(211)\nWA MAA YAMBAGHEE LAHUM WA MAA YASTATEE-O’ON.\nNeither does it behoove them, nor are they capable [of doing that].\nاِنَّهُمْ عَنِ السَّمْعِ لَمَعْزُوْلُوْنَؕ‏(212)\nINNAHUM A’NIS SAM-E’ LA-MA’ZOOLOON.\nIndeed, they are kept at bay [even] from hearing it.\nفَلَا تَدْعُ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ فَتَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُعَذَّبِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(213)\nFALAA TAD-O’ MA-A’L LAAHE ELAAHAN AAKHARA FA-TAKOONA MENAL MO-A’ZZABEEN.\nSo do not invoke any god besides Allah, lest you should be among the punished.\nوَاَنْذِرْ عَشِيْرَتَكَ الْاَقْرَبِيْنَۙ‏(214)\nWA ANZIR A’SHEERATAKAL AQRABEEN.\nWarn the nearest of your kinsfolk,\nوَاخْفِضْ جَنَاحَكَ لِمَنِ اتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(215)\nWAKH FIZ JANAAHAKA LEMANIT TABA-A’KA MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nand lower your wing to the faithful who follow you.\nفَاِنْ عَصَوْكَ فَقُلْ اِنِّىْ بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(216)\nFA-IN A’SAWKA FA-QUL INNEE BAREE-UM MIMMAA TA’MALOON.\nBut if they disobey you, say, ‘I am absolved of what you do.’\nوَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى الْعَزِيْزِ الرَّحِيْمِۙ‏(217)\nWA TAWAKKAL A’LAL A’ZEEZIR RAHEEM.\nAnd put your trust in the All-mighty, the All-merciful,\nالَّذِىْ يَرٰٮكَ حِيْنَ تَقُوْمُۙ‏(218)\nLAZEE YARAAKA HEENA TAQOOM.\nwho sees you when you stand [for prayer],\nوَتَقَلُّبَكَ فِى السّٰجِدِيْنَ‏(219)\nWA TAQALLOBAKA FIS SAAJEDEEN.\nand your going about among those who prostrate.\nاِنَّهٗ هُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(220)\nINNAHU HOWAS SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nIndeed He is the All-hearing, the All-knowing.\nهَلْ اُنَبِّئُكُمْ عَلٰى مَنْ تَنَزَّلُ الشَّيٰطِيْنُؕ‏(221)\nHAL ONABBE-OKUM A’LAA MAN TANAZZALUSH SHAYAATEEN.\nShould I inform you on whom the devils descend?\nتَنَزَّلُ عَلٰى كُلِّ اَفَّاكٍ اَثِيْمٍۙ‏(222)\nTANAZZALO A’LAA KULLE AFFAAKIN ASEEM.\nThey descend on every sinful liar.\nيُّلْقُوْنَ السَّمْعَ وَاَكْثَرُهُمْ كٰذِبُوْنَؕ‏(223)\nYULQOONAS SAM-A’ WA AKSAROHUM KAAZEBOON.\nThey eavesdrop, and most of them are liars.\nوَالشُّعَرَآءُ يَتَّبِعُهُمُ الْغَاوٗنَؕ‏(224)\nWASH SHO-A’RAAA-O YATTABE-O’HOMUL GHAAWOON.\nAs for the poets, [only] the perverse follow them.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّهُمْ فِىْ كُلِّ وَادٍ يَّهِيْمُوْنَۙ‏(225)\nALAM TARA ANNAHUM FEE KULLE WAADIN-Y YAHEEMOON.\nHave you not regarded that they rove in every valley,\nوَاَنَّهُمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ مَا لَا يَفْعَلُوْنَۙ‏(226)\nWA ANNAHUM YAQOOLOONA MAA LAA YAF-A’LOON.\nand that they say what they do not do?\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَذَكَرُوا اللّٰهَ كَثِيْرًا وَّانْتَصَرُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا ظُلِمُوْا‌ ؕ وَسَيَعْلَمُ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْۤا اَىَّ مُنْقَلَبٍ يَّنْقَلِبُوْنَ‏(227)\nILLAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WA ZAKARUL LAAHA KASEERANW WAN TASAROO MIM BA’DE MAA ZOLEMOO, WA SAYA’LAMUL LAZEENA ZALAMOO AYYA MUNQALABIN-Y YANQALEBOON.\nBarring those who have faith, do righteous deeds, and remember Allah much often, and vindicate themselves after they have been wronged. And the wrongdoers will soon know at what goal they will end up.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Shoaraa (The Poets)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has a total of 227 verses. In the commentary of Burhan it is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites the three Tawaseen (i.e. the three Surahs beginning with Taa-Seen) on every Thursday night, will be counted from the friends of Allah and will be under the protection of Allah (s.w.t.). The reward for reciting this Surah is so great that when the person sees the reward he has gotten from it (on the Day of Judgement) he will be pleased.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the one who recites this Surah will come out of his grave reciting the Shahadah or Kalimah, bearing witness in the Oneness of Allah (s.w.t.). Reciting Surah al-Shoaraa at dawn is compared to the recitation of all the heavenly books that have been revealed. Frequent recitation of this Surah ensures protection from thieves and from death by drowning or being burnt. Drinking water in which this Surah was dissolved protects one from all types of ailments."
